% Origin: Kowalski, *Computational Logic and Human Thinking*,
%         Chapter 5, section 5.7 ("Housing Benefit rule and exception").
% Last verification: no open issues (no errors/warnings; all tests pass).
%
% Rules-and-exceptions with negation as failure. A person gets help to pay rent
% if the person receives housing benefit. Receiving housing benefit holds when
% any one of three eligibility paths applies (on other benefits, works part-time,
% works full-time on a low income) AND the person is not ineligible. To avoid
% and/or precedence trouble, the disjunctive "receives housing benefit" rule is
% SPLIT into three single-disjunct clauses, each carrying the same
% "it is not the case that ... is ineligible" exception condition. A person is
% ineligible if not on a low income.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
*a person* gets help to pay rent.
*a person* receives housing benefit.
*a person* is on other benefits.
*a person* works part-time.
*a person* works full-time on a low income.
*a person* is on a low income.
*a person* is ineligible to receive housing benefit.

the knowledge base housing benefit includes:

a person gets help to pay rent
    if the person receives housing benefit.

a person receives housing benefit
    if the person is on other benefits
    and it is not the case that
        the person is ineligible to receive housing benefit.

a person receives housing benefit
    if the person works part-time
    and it is not the case that
        the person is ineligible to receive housing benefit.

a person receives housing benefit
    if the person works full-time on a low income
    and it is not the case that
        the person is ineligible to receive housing benefit.

a person is ineligible to receive housing benefit
    if it is not the case that
        the person is on a low income.

scenario claimants is:
    bob is on other benefits.
    bob is on a low income.
    mary works part-time.
    mary is on a low income.
    tom works full-time on a low income.
    tom is on a low income.
    rich works part-time.
    help expects answers ["bob gets help to pay rent", "mary gets help to pay rent", "tom gets help to pay rent"].

query help is:
    which person gets help to pay rent.
